title HUNK81 — the part detail page: a tapped ref paints the picture above its full facts
prompt continue the recursion after HUNK80; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve, send as its own signed round to origin and xykj61, stop at custody gates
think HUNK80 closed the loop up to the tap — a keeper narrows the shelf, touches a result, gets a PartRef — yet the tap opened onto nothing to SEE. A shelf row is a one-line glance; a real catalog's detail page is larger, the picture bigger, each fact on its own line. The next durable crux is painting that page from the handle HUNK80 hands over, so the gesture arrives: search -> tap -> the part's own page.
think Chose pure painting over surfaces already proven — detail_page(cat, ref, cols, rows, pic_rows) renders the part's window (cat.render_part), down-maps it into the top band, and stacks the four facts (name, part number, material, exact price via part_row.format_price) below. The crux is NO DRIFT: picture and every fact line read the same ref + catalog, so one product's picture can never sit beside another's price.
think First build panicked in down_map's partition assert (x1 > x0): down_map only DOWNSAMPLES, and a 4-px-wide window cannot fill a 48-col band — an empty partition. Fixed by mirroring paint_swatch's stretch idiom in 2D: down-map to the window's own size (min(cols,width) x min(pic_rows,height)), then stretch across the page band by src = (r*ph/pic_rows, c*pw/cols). A picture wider than its window never empties a partition.
obs Durable property proven on metal over four parts in known color bands: bolt's page paints a red picture band (slot 3) above bolt/HX-M8-40/stainless-304/$1.25, gear's a blue band (slot 5) above gear/$8.45 — each fact line EQUAL to the stored fact, a different part a different picture and different facts (no drift). The page rasterizes to a lit canvas. EmptyPage, PageTooLarge, EmptyPicture, PageTooShort each refuse by name.
obs The capstone ties HUNK80 to HUNK81 end to end: open_tapped_and on a stainless-only search's second row resolves to hexnut (orig index 3, across the narrowing), and detail_page over that ref paints hexnut's own picture and facts ($0.55) — search to tap to detail. A price is a fact formatted for reading, never moved — custody gate #3 untouched. No network, no key, no funds. TAME bans clean, width exit 0; HUNK80 tap and HUNK73/74 row helpers stay GREEN beneath.
loom witness=hunk_part_detail_witness parts=4 pic_rows=4 fact_rows=4 capstone=search_tap_detail_hexnut
file brushstroke/part_detail.rye HUNK81 — paint a tapped part's detail page (picture band stretched over the window, four fact rows)
